Blue: Wild Variant (WV)</note>
    <note x="30" y="359" height="240" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="18" width="261" markdown="false" textColorLight="-1664597" backgroundLight="0">In the simulation, survival rate and reproductive rate are represented using decimal values between 0 and 1. These decimals represent probabilities. For example, a value of 0.2 means there is a 20% chance of survival or reproduction, while 1.0 represents 100%.</note>
